# Component Library Architecture

Atlas Design System monorepo. **CSS Modules only** — no Tailwind.

**Framework: React / CSS Modules**

See also: `package-exports-tree-shaking` (export map and barrels), `update-docs-on-completed-work` (where to document components, utilities, and hooks).

## Stack

- React 19, TypeScript, Biome (2-space indent)
- Turborepo workspaces: `apps/*`, `packages/*`
- Colors: `@spiffdog-design/atlas-colors` (OKLab palette scales with `light-dark()`)
- Components: `@spiffdog-design/atlas-components`
- Utilities and hooks: `@spiffdog-design/atlas-tools` — utilities from root or `./utilities/*`; hooks from `./hooks/*`
- Docs: Storybook in `apps/docs` (stories colocated in `packages/atlas-components/src` and `packages/atlas-colors/src/preview`)
- Headless UI (when native HTML/CSS is insufficient): `@base-ui/react` — behavior/a11y only; never reimplement dialogs, menus, focus traps
- Tests: Vitest + Testing Library; Storybook for all shared components

```ts
import { Button } from "@spiffdog-design/atlas-components/button";
import { palette } from "@spiffdog-design/atlas-colors";
import { useUrlQuery } from "@spiffdog-design/atlas-tools/hooks/use-url-query";
import "@spiffdog-design/atlas-components/styles.css";
```

Storybook resolves package imports via Vite aliases in `apps/docs/.storybook/main.ts`.

## Visual theme and atmosphere

Restrained monochrome: near-white canvas (`--color-bg` / `--gray11`), near-black text (`--color-text` / `--gray1`). Every element earns its placement — minimalism as engineering principle, not decoration.

- **Border-edge rings** — use `--border-edge` box-shadow rings instead of `1px border` on all shared components (cleaner rounded corners); stack elevation shadows separately
- **Optical alignment** — ±1px nudge when perception beats geometry
- Set `<meta name="theme-color">` to match page background; rely on `color-scheme: light dark` on `:root`

## Monorepo layout

```
apps/docs/                       # Storybook — MDX docs + preview config
packages/
  atlas-colors/                  # Palette tokens (TS + CSS custom properties)
  atlas-components/              # Shared React components
    src/
      styles/                    # index.css, tokens.css, globals.css
      button/                    # Per-component folder
      index.ts
  atlas-tools/                   # Utilities and React hooks
    src/
      utilities/                 # Pure helpers (array, string, urlQuery.utils, …)
      hooks/                     # React hooks (useUrlQuery, …)
  biome-config/
  typescript-config/
```

Per component (e.g. `packages/atlas-components/src/button/`):

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `index.tsx` | React component — JSX, hooks, handlers that delegate to utils |
| `button.module.css` | Layered CSS Module styles |
| `button.stories.tsx` | Storybook (`atlas components/Button`) — **required** |
| `button.utils.ts` | Pure functions — validation, formatters, type guards, defaults |
| `button.test.ts` | Vitest unit tests for **every export** in `button.utils.ts` |

Per utility module (`packages/atlas-tools/src/utilities/`): TSDoc on exports + `{module}.test.ts`.

Per hook (`packages/atlas-tools/src/hooks/{name}/`): TSDoc on hook and providers + tests + README hooks table entry.

## Styling rules

1. **CSS cascade layers** — declared in `packages/atlas-components/src/styles/index.css`:
   ```css
   @layer theme, components, variants, vendor;
   ```
   | Layer | Contents | Priority |
   |-------|----------|----------|
   | `theme` | atlas-colors, `tokens.css`, `globals.css` | lowest |
   | `components` | shared component structure in `*.module.css` | |
   | `variants` | `data-*` props and headless UI state in `*.module.css` | |
   | `vendor` | third-party library overrides | |
   | *(unlayered)* | consumer app `*.module.css`, ad-hoc UI tweaks | **highest** |

2. **CSS Modules** for all component styles. Global CSS only via layered imports in `styles/index.css`. Storybook uses `localsConvention: "camelCaseOnly"`.
3. **Data-attributes for styling variants only** — map **styling props** (`appearance`, `variant`, affirmative booleans like `rounded`) to `data-*` in `@layer variants`. **Never emit `data-*="false"`** — omit the attribute when inactive so CSS defaults apply cleanly.
4. **Prefer native and ARIA attributes for behavior/state** — use `disabled`, `required`, `checked`, `aria-*`, etc. on the DOM element instead of mirroring them in `data-*`. Do not set `data-disabled` on Atlas wrappers; style native `:disabled` (or `:checked`, `:invalid`, …) where the platform provides it.
5. **Headless UI library state** — when `@base-ui/react` sets `data-disabled`, `data-checked`, `data-highlighted`, etc., style those selectors in `@layer variants`; do not duplicate the same state with Atlas-owned `data-*` props.
6. **Static classes only in JS** — join `styles.root` and passthrough `className`; no variant toggles in JS.
7. **Use tokens** from `styles/tokens.css` for spacing, sizing, color, radius, and typography.
8. **Border-edge over `border`** — never use `1px solid` for component outlines. Set `border: none` and draw edges with box-shadow via `--border-edge` tokens from `tokens.css`:
   ```css
   .root {
     border: none;
     box-shadow: var(--border-edge, var(--border-edge-default));
   }

   .root[data-variant="outline"] {
     --border-edge: var(--border-edge-primary);
   }

   .root:disabled {
     --border-edge: var(--border-edge-subtle);
   }
   ```
   Preset tokens: `--border-edge` (neutral mix), `--border-edge-default`, `--border-edge-subtle`, `--border-edge-primary`, `--border-edge-inner` (inset tracks/wells). Override `--border-edge` per variant/state; stack `--shadow-subtle` / `--shadow-float` as separate comma-separated layers — do not merge focus into edge shadow.
9. **Focus rings stay on `outline`** — `:focus-visible` uses `outline: var(--focus-ring)` + `outline-offset: var(--focus-ring-offset)`, not a second box-shadow layer (unless a component already documents an exception).
10. **Nested radii** — child `border-radius` ≤ parent; concentric curves.

## Typography

Target stack in `tokens.css`:

```css
--font-family-sans: "Inter", system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
```

| Topic | Guidance |
|-------|----------|
| OpenType | `font-feature-settings: "liga" 1` globally; `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` for numeric columns |
| Wrapping | `text-wrap: balance` or `text-wrap: pretty` on headings |
| Tracking | Display headings: modest negative `letter-spacing` in em (e.g. `-0.02em` to `-0.04em`); never positive letter-spacing on headings |
| Scale | Define `--font-size-*` with `clamp()` — e.g. display `clamp(3.2rem, 2.5vw + 2rem, 4.8rem)`, body median `1.4rem`–`1.6rem` |
| Mobile inputs | **`font-size: 1.6rem` minimum** on `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>` (prevents iOS Safari zoom; valid with `html { font-size: 62.5% }`) |
| Weights | 400 body, 500–600 UI labels/buttons, 600–700 display |

## Copywriting

- Active voice, 2nd person ("Install the CLI")
- Title Case for headings and buttons; sentence case on marketing prose
- Numerals for counts; non-breaking space between numbers and units
- Real ellipsis `…`, curly quotes, `&` when space-constrained
- Specific button labels ("Save API Key" not "Continue")
- Constructive errors with exit path — state the problem and how to fix it

See `design-philosophy` for Storybook copy tone.

## Colors and tokens

**Palette** (`@spiffdog-design/atlas-colors`) — raw scales as `--{palette}{step}`. Components use semantic `--color-*`, not raw steps.

| Role | Atlas token |
|------|-------------|
| Primary text / dark surface | `--gray1` → `--color-text` |
| Page / card surface | `--gray12` → `--color-bg`, `--color-surface` |
| Primary / develop / link accent | `--blue6` → `--color-primary` |
| Focus ring | `--blue8` → `--color-focus-ring` |
| Ship / destructive accent | `--tomato6` or `--red6` |
| Preview accent | `--fuchsia6` |
| Console / syntax blue | `--blue7` |
| Console purple | `--violet6` |
| Console pink | `--ruby6` |
| Inner highlight (shadow stack) | `--gray11` |
| Border edge (neutral ring) | `--border-edge` |
| Border edge (semantic) | `--border-edge-default`, `--border-edge-subtle`, `--border-edge-primary`, `--border-edge-success`, `--border-edge-warning`, `--border-edge-error` |
| Inset well edge | `--border-edge-inner`, `--border-edge-inner-muted` |

Interactive states: `:hover`, `:active`, `:focus-visible` must increase contrast vs rest; never rely on color alone — include text labels.

**Rem scale**: `html { font-size: 62.5%; }` → **1rem = 10px**.

Token categories in `tokens.css`: `--space-*`, `--control-height-*`, `--font-size-*`, `--radius-*`, `--color-*`, `--border-edge*`, `--focus-ring`.

- Padding/margin/gap → `--space-*`; colors → `--color-*`; radius → `--radius-*`; edges → `--border-edge*`
- **OK to hardcode**: `2px` outline width, `999px` pill radius, `0`/`100%`/`fit-content`
- **Do not** use `border: 1px solid` on shared components — use `--border-edge` tokens
- **Do not** duplicate token values as literals — add to `tokens.css` when reused

## Depth, elevation, and borders

- Two-layer shadows (ambient + direct) for elevation — `--shadow-float`, `--shadow-subtle`, `--shadow-raised`
- Component outlines → `--border-edge*` rings (`border: none`); elevation shadows are separate layers in `box-shadow`
- Nested radii: child radius ≤ parent radius

## Components and interactions

### Forms

- **Field composition** — labeled controls use `@base-ui/react/field` via shared `FormField` (`packages/atlas-components/src/shared/form-field.tsx`). Accept `label?`, `description?`, and `error?` on every Field-wrapped component (Input, Checkbox, Select, …). Part order: `Field.Label` → control → `Field.Description` → `Field.Error`. Never use plain `<p>` or `<span>` for helper or error copy — always `Field.Description` / `Field.Error`. Static `error` props use `<Field.Error match>`. Reuse field chrome from `shared/form-field.module.css` (`.field`, `.label`, `.description`, `.error`). Pass Base UI control primitives as `FormField` children so labels and descriptions wire up correctly.
- Generous hit targets; if visual target &lt;24px, expand to ≥24px via padding
- Label + control share a single hit target
- **Never block paste**; validate instead of blocking keystrokes
- Placeholders end with `…` and show example patterns
- Submit stays enabled until flight; then disable, show spinner, keep original label; ~150–300ms show-delay on fast responses
- Mobile form controls: **`font-size: 1.6rem` minimum**

### Links and buttons

- `<a href>` for navigation; `<button type="button">` for actions — never `<div onClick>` for routing
- Preserve Cmd/Ctrl+click on links

### Skeletons, tooltips, drag and drop

- Skeletons mirror final layout exactly (no CLS)
- Delay first tooltip in a group; instant for subsequent peers
- Drag: `user-select: none` + `inert` on dragged elements

## Platform-first behavior

**Prefer native HTML and CSS** for interaction, state, and accessibility. JavaScript is **progressive enhancement**.

### Priority order

1. **Semantic HTML**
2. **CSS** — pseudo-classes, attribute selectors, modern platform CSS
3. **Declarative DOM** — `data-*` and native attributes
4. **JavaScript** — only when platform primitives are insufficient; delegate a11y-heavy patterns to `@base-ui/react`

### Prefer native primitives

| Need | Reach for | Not first |
|------|-----------|-----------|
| Disclosure / accordion | `details`/`summary`, `hidden` | `useState` + click toggles |
| Modal / alert | `<dialog>`, `form[method="dialog"]` | Portal + manual focus trap |
| Form validation | `required`, `pattern`, `type`, `:invalid` | Custom validators before native fails |
| Toggle / selection | `checkbox`, `radio`, `select`, `:checked` | `onClick` + boolean state for styling |
| Navigation | `<a href>`, `<button type="button">` | `div` + `onClick` |

### Modern CSS platform features

Prefer anchor positioning, `@container`, `@starting-style`, `subgrid`, `color-mix()`, `light-dark()`, `field-sizing: content`, and other evergreen platform features over bespoke JS.

### Component wrappers

React components are **thin adapters**: correct semantic markup, `data-*`/native attributes, JS only where the platform falls short. Testable logic lives in `{name}.utils.ts`.

## Layout and performance

- Flex/Grid over JS measurement; no layout reads in render
- `env(safe-area-inset-*)` for full-bleed layouts
- **URL-persisted UI state** — filters, tabs, pagination, expanded panels via `useUrlQuery` + router-specific providers (not `useState` alone for shareable config):
  ```tsx
  import { useUrlQuery } from "@spiffdog-design/atlas-tools/hooks/use-url-query";
  import { ReactRouterUrlQueryProvider } from "@spiffdog-design/atlas-tools/hooks/use-url-query/react-router";
  // Native (no router): import { NativeUrlQueryProvider } from ".../hooks/use-url-query/native-router";
  ```
  Wrap the app in a provider, or pass `options.source`. The core hook does not default to any adapter.
- `overflow-x: hidden` where needed; `overscroll-behavior: contain` in modals/drawers
- Virtualize lists &gt;50 items (`content-visibility: auto` or virtualization lib)
- Preload critical fonts (`rel="preload"`, `font-display: swap`) and above-fold images (`fetchpriority="high"`, explicit dimensions)
- `min-width: 0` on flex children for text truncation

## Animation and motion

- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`
- Never `transition: all` — list properties explicitly
- Interruptible animations; no autoplay
- SVG: transform wrapper + `transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center`

## Accessibility

- Mandatory `:focus-visible` ring via `--focus-ring`; never `outline: none` without replacement; use `:focus-within` for groups
- Set required **ARIA and native attributes** on the correct element (`aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby`, `aria-invalid`, `aria-expanded`, `disabled`, `required`, …) — do not replace them with custom `data-*` mirrors
- Icon-only buttons: `aria-label`; images: meaningful `alt` or `alt=""`; decorative icons: `aria-hidden="true"`
- Async updates: `aria-live="polite"` for toasts, loading, inline validation
- i18n: `translate="no"` on brand/code tokens; `Intl.*` for dates and numbers
- Every form control gets `<label>` or `aria-label`

## Storybook

- `npm run dev` from repo root or `apps/docs`
- Story titles: `atlas components/{Name}`, `atlas colors/{Name}`
- Preview imports `@spiffdog-design/atlas-components/styles/index.css`
- **Required** for every shared component: `{name}.stories.tsx` (see `update-docs-on-completed-work`)

## Pure logic and testing

Extract testable logic into `{name}.utils.ts` or `atlas-tools` utilities. **Unit tests required** for every export from utils modules.

Also required for every shared component: `*.stories.tsx`. Optional: `*.test.tsx` for render/a11y tests.

## Agent prompt guide

**Quick Tech Stack and Rules**

- Framework: **React / CSS Modules**
- Typography: Inter, `"liga"`, tabular nums, `text-wrap: balance`
- Spacing/layout: Flex/Grid, `min-width: 0` on flex children
- State: **`useUrlQuery`** for URL-driven UI config
- Imports: prefer subpaths (`/button`, `/utilities/string`, `/hooks/use-url-query`) for tree-shaking

**Example prompts**

- *"Create a hero section. Headline uses `--font-size-display` clamp, `text-wrap: balance`, modest negative letter-spacing. CTA is native `<button>`, keeps label but shows spinner on submit. Card uses `--border-edge-subtle` + `--shadow-subtle`."*
- *"Build an API key input. Explicit `<label>`, `font-size: 1.6rem`, autocomplete='off', placeholder ending in '…', allows paste. Focus uses `--focus-ring`."*
- *"Design a card grid. Cards use multi-layer shadow tokens. Wrap routable cards in `<a href>`. Persist filter tab in URL via `useUrlQuery`."*

## Do not

- Add Tailwind or utility-first CSS frameworks
- Use `nuqs` or third-party query-string libs when `useUrlQuery` covers the need
- Put variant styles in global CSS or inline styles
- Hardcode spacing/sizing/color/radius when a token exists
- Skip stories, TSDoc, or `{name}.test.ts` for new shared artifacts
- Inline testable logic in `index.tsx` instead of utils modules
- Use `@mui/base` (deprecated) — use `@base-ui/react`
- Reimplement in JS what native HTML/CSS already provides
- Use non-semantic elements as interactive controls when a native element exists
- Use positive letter-spacing on display type
- Use `transition: all` or animate layout properties (`width`, `height`, `top`)
- Block paste or disable zoom (`maximum-scale=1`, `user-scalable=no`)
- Use `<div>` for links or `<a>` for button actions
- Use `autoFocus` on mobile
